================================================================================
Sources, Protocol Specifications, and Third-Party Notices
================================================================================

1. MAVLink Wire Protocol & Microservices Specifications (v1 & v2)
   - Wire Serialization & Field Reordering: https://mavlink.io/en/guide/serialization.html
   - Packet Signing (SHA-256 13-Byte Signature): https://mavlink.io/en/guide/message_signing.html
   - X.25 CRC-16/MCRF4XX & CRC_EXTRA Seed: https://mavlink.io/en/guide/crc.html
   - Microservices (Heartbeat, Parameter, Mission, Command, Timesync): https://mavlink.io/en/services/
   - Relationship: This library is a clean-room native MoonBit implementation
     (100% pure MoonBit, Zero FFI) of the MAVLink v2 and v1 binary wire framing,
     ITU-T X.25 CRC-16/MCRF4XX checksum, payload trailing-zero truncation,
     FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 packet signing, stateful microservice state machines,
     and recursive multi-file `<include>` XML schema code generator.

2. Official MAVLink XML Message Definitions (`minimal.xml`, `common.xml`)
   - Upstream Repository: https://github.com/mavlink/mavlink
   - Upstream Reference C Library: https://github.com/mavlink/c_library_v2
   - Upstream Copyright: Copyright (c) 2009-2026 Lorenz Meier and MAVLink Contributors
   - Upstream License: MIT License / CC0-1.0 (https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
   - Usage: Official XML message definitions (45 standard flight messages and
     18 standard enums from `minimal.xml` and `common.xml`) and their reference
     `CRC_EXTRA` seed constants are embedded in `xml_catalog.mbt` and
     `benchmark.mbt` as input schemas for self-hosted MoonBit code generation
     (`standard_dialect.mbt`) and golden wire vector conformance verification.

3. Cryptographic & Checksum Standard Test Vectors
   - NIST FIPS PUB 180-4 (Secure Hash Standard, SHA-256 single-block and multi-block vectors)
   - ITU-T Recommendation X.25 / ISO/IEC 13239 (`CRC-16/MCRF4XX` check value `0x906E` for `"123456789"`)
